	abstract = {The energy relations in an optical cavity are studied, beginning with a simple derivation of the relation between the field transmission and reflection coefficients at an interface, based upon time-reversal symmetry. Using this, the size and frequency dependence of the internal and reflected fields and intensities for standing-wave and traveling-wave cavities are derived. Resonator Q, finesse, photon lifetime and impedance matching into a cavity are then discussed. A novel technique is described for coupling radiation into a cavity using an intracavity transparent wedge. The chapter concludes with a discussion of some practical matters, such as the experimental determination of certain cavity parameters.},
