	isbn = {978-0-19-966548-8},
	url = {https://doi.org/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199665488.003.0001},
	abstract = {A full description of Gaussian beams is given, based upon solutions to the “paraxial wave equation”, which describes the propagation of electromagnetic waves in homogeneous media when the normals to the wavefronts make a very small angle to some symmetry axis of the system. The beams are completely described by the complex beam parameter, q, which can be used to analyze the passage of Gaussian beams through laboratory apparatus. A better and simpler analysis tool is the “ABCD rule”, which facilitates the study of Gaussian beams in the presence of optical elements such as lenses, spherical mirrors and crystals for laser gain or nonlinear optics.},
